0..71 Comment "// Loops and their exits. A `loop` or a `while` may run forever, so the"
72..151 Comment "// function holding one states `Partial` in its row, `-F [Partial] T`: the host"
152..229 Comment "// interface with no operation, which nothing handles (#1481). A caller holds"
230..310 Comment "// it in its own row, and an entry runs at `+U (-F [Partial] T)`. A `for` over a"
311..385 Comment "// list descends on the list and needs no entry; each `become` is an exit."
387..414 Comment "// The native finite lists."
